{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_3ecaef21e59d4e11a692f456","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Key detail: the runner's `ClaudeResult.Result` is the raw text. The step parses the last JSON object from it as AgentResult. If the envelope has status done and `output`, it writes the `output` field (heading-stripped) as the section body. If status needs_input/failed, returns that status without writing the section.\n\nSo fake runner responses should be JSON envelopes: `{\"status\":\"done\",\"output\":\"...\"}`. The task says \"The fake runner returns, in order: a plan, then a High verdict...\". So the `output` contains the section body (the actual plan/verdict text). Let me look at how existing prompt/step tests build these envelopes, or the AgentResult struct.\n\nLet me check AgentResult struct and BuildPrompt for Environment section.","signature":"llm-proxy"}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65223de2-d5ca-493e-b6ca-024741641a7c","uuid":"5ddf1189-7380-4e3a-80ae-f438bd13c477","timestamp":"2026-11-26T19:03:17.531Z"}
