{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba07d73a7edaf702","type":"tool_result","content":"# Changelog\n\nAll notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.\n\nPlease choose versions by [Semantic Versioning](http://semver.org/).\n\n* MAJOR version when you make incompatible API changes,\n* MINOR version when you add functionality in a backwards-compatible manner, and\n* PATCH version when you make backwards-compatible bug fixes.\n\n## Unreleased\n\n- feat: Add `agent/scripts/repo-clone.sh`, the fourth read-only observation script, cloning a public GitHub repo into the fixed `repos/` directory beside `scripts/` and reporting `clone_path`, `head_sha` and `default_branch` [rejects any reference that is not `owner/name`, resolves the destination with symlinks followed and refuses anything outside `repos/` before git runs or the filesystem is touched, then makes the clone non-writable]\n- feat: Wire the observation scripts' endpoints through `CLAUDE_ENV` and align the Config allowlist, image and prose with the four scripts that exist [drops the non-existent `pod-logs.sh` entry, adds `git` to the runtime image, and adds `pkg/scripts/consistency_test.go` to fail `make test` when the allowlist, the scripts on disk and the docs disagree]\n\n## v0.2.2\n\n- chore: remove orphaned section comments left in `.trivyignore` by the stale-ignore sweep\n\n## v0.2.1\n\n- chore: remove 9 stale vulnerability ignores (withdrawn advisory, module absent from go.mod, or version outside the affected range)\n- chore: install Trivy from a pinned release tarball in CI so the job no longer depends on the retired apt-key helper\n\n## v0.2.0\n\n- feat: add a `check-task-link` gate that fails a PR whose body carries no `Task: <task_identifier>` line, and install Trivy from the upstream script so `test` stops failing on the retired keyring helper\n\n## v0.1.5\n\n- chore: bump `ERRCHECK_VERSION` to v1.30.0 and `GOSEC_VERSION` to v2.30.0. The pinned versions could not type-check the Go 1.27 stdlib, and these stay in step with the canonical `tools.env`.\n\n## v0.1.4\n\n- chore: update Go to 1.27.4 and github.com/bborbe/agent to v0.141.1, github.com/bborbe/cqrs to v0.6.16, github.com/bborbe/errors to v1.6.7, github.com/bborbe/kafka to v1.29.14, github.com/bborbe/sentry to v1.10.8, github.com/bborbe/service to v1.11.4, github.com/bborbe/time to v1.27.28, github.com/bborbe/vault-cli to v0.192.4\n\n## v0.1.3\n\n- chore: restate the do-not-merge contract in the gate workflow\n\n===README env sections===\n45:### Config CRD env pattern\n66:### Claude subprocess env allowlist","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65223de2-d5ca-493e-b6ca-024741641a7c","uuid":"f9b394ff-0f97-4713-b174-c2b175bfc222","timestamp":"2026-11-26T19:03:52.451Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Changelog\n\nAll notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.\n\nPlease choose versions by [Semantic Versioning](http://semver.org/).\n\n* MAJOR version when you make incompatible API changes,\n* MINOR version when you add functionality in a backwards-compatible manner, and\n* PATCH version when you make backwards-compatible bug fixes.\n\n## Unreleased\n\n- feat: Add `agent/scripts/repo-clone.sh`, the fourth read-only observation script, cloning a public GitHub repo into the fixed `repos/` directory beside `scripts/` and reporting `clone_path`, `head_sha` and `default_branch` [rejects any reference that is not `owner/name`, resolves the destination with symlinks followed and refuses anything outside `repos/` before git runs or the filesystem is touched, then makes the clone non-writable]\n- feat: Wire the observation scripts' endpoints through `CLAUDE_ENV` and align the Config allowlist, image and prose with the four scripts that exist [drops the non-existent `pod-logs.sh` entry, adds `git` to the runtime image, and adds `pkg/scripts/consistency_test.go` to fail `make test` when the allowlist, the scripts on disk