{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_ca7cf11912204fb2be022d68","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Build passes. Now write the two test files. Let me plan the phase_chain_test.go carefully.\n\nLet me design helpers:\n\n```go\npackage factory_test\n\nimport (\n    \"context\"\n    \"encoding/json\"\n    \"os\"\n    \"path/filepath\"\n    \"strings\"\n\n    agentlib \"github.com/bborbe/agent\"\n    claudelib \"github.com/bborbe/agent/claude\"\n    delivery \"github.com/bborbe/agent/delivery\"\n    agentmocks \"github.com/bborbe/agent/mocks\"\n    . \"github.com/onsi/ginkgo/v2\"\n    . \"github.com/onsi/gomega\"\n\n    \"github.com/bborbe/defect-diagnoser-agent/pkg/factory\"\n)\n```\n\nConstants:\n- service = \"checkout\"\n- repo = \"bborbe/foo\"\n- fixturePath = \"pkg/x/y.go\"\n- fixtureRepoContent = \"line one\\nline two\\nline three\\n\" (3 lines)\n- evidence = \"scripts/prometheus-query.sh 'rate(http_requests_total{code=\\\"500\\\"}[5m])'\\n{\\\"status\\\":\\\"success\\\"}\"\n\nEnvelope builders:\n\n```go\nfunc doneEnvelope(output string) *claudelib.ClaudeResult {\n    b, err := json.Marshal(map[string]string{\"status\":\"done\",\"output\":output})\n    Expect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n    return &claudelib.ClaudeResult{Result: string(b)}\n}\nfunc statusEnvelope(status, message string) *claudelib.ClaudeResult {\n    b, _ := json.Marshal(map[string]string{\"status\":status,\"message\":message})\n    return &claudelib.ClaudeResult{Result: string(b)}\n}\n```\n\nActually `message` for needs_input. Use struct or map.\n\nPlan output:\n```go\nfunc planOutput() string {\n    return \"## Plan\\n\\nservice: checkout\\nrepo: bborbe/foo\\nclone_path: /tmp/repos/bborbe/foo\\nhead_sha: abc123\\n\"\n}\n```\nNo column-0 # other than the leading ## Plan which is stripped. Wait — stripLeadingSectionHeading drops a leading \"## \" heading and one following blank line. So body becomes \"service: checkout\\n...\". Fine, and wrapper writes under ## Plan. Assertion only checks section presence/order.\n\nReview output: \"review passed; no new findings.\\n\" — no column-0 #.\n\nVerdict output: fenced yaml with eight keys. Build:\n```go\nfunc verdictOutput(fields map[string]string) string {\n    return \"```yaml\\n\" + buildYAML(fields) + \"```\\n\"\n}\n```\nUse yaml? Simpler manual. But values with newlines (evidence) need block scalar. I'll write helper similar to verdict tests.\n\nActually easier: build the yaml block manually using yaml.Marshal of a yaml.Node? Simpler: evidence contains newline. Use a literal block:\n\n```yaml\ndefect_id: defect-1\nservice: checkout\nrepo: bborbe/foo\nfile:line: pkg/x/y.go:3\nroot_cause: the handler dereferences a nil pointer\nrecommended_fix: guard the nil pointer\nevidence: |\n  scripts/prometheus-query.sh '...'\n  {\"status\":\"success\"}\nconfidence: High\n```\n\nThis parses. Good.\n\nNow task fixture builder:\n\n```go\nfunc taskDocument(phase string, extraBody string) string {\n    return `---\ntask_type: defect-diagnose\nphase: ` + phase + `\nstatus: in_progress\nassignee: defect-diagnoser-agent\ndefect_id: defect-1\ntrigger_count: 1\nmax_triggers: 3\n---\n\n## Observation\n\nthe checkout service returns 500s\n` + extraBody\n}\n```\n\nFor case (a), extraBody = \"\\n## Failure\\n\\n- **Reason:**\\n\\n```\\nstale\\n```\\n\" placed after ## Observation. Good.\n\nFor case (j), phase ai_review and body includes a pre-written ## Verdict section with Medium. Also no ## Plan (not needed since entry ai_review). Body = observation + \"\\n## Verdict\\n\\n\" + verdictOutput(mediumFields). The step ShouldRun for ai_review: output section ## Review absent → runs. Fine.\n\nHarness function:\n\n```go\ntype chainCase struct {\n    phase     string\n    body      string\n    responses []*claudelib.ClaudeResult\n    env       map[string]string  // optional\n    verdictLine int // expected\n}\n```\n\nActually let me write a helper `runChain(responses, taskContent string) (string, *agentmocks.ClaudeRunner)`:\n\n```go\nfunc runChain(taskContent string, responses ...*claudelib.ClaudeResult) (string, *agentmocks.ClaudeRunner) {\n    tmp := GinkgoT().TempDir()  // or os.MkdirTemp\n    writeFixtureClone(tmp)\n    fake := &agentmocks.ClaudeRunner{}\n    fake.RunReturns(statusEnvelope(\"failed\", \"unexpected extra model call\"))\n    for i, r := range responses {\n        fake.RunReturnsOnCall(i, r, nil)\n    }\n    env := map[string]string{\"service_repo.\" + service: repo}\n    agent := factory.CreateAgentFromRunner(fake, claudelib.AgentDir(tmp), env)\n    taskPath := filepath.Join(GinkgoT().TempDir(), \"task.md\")\n    Expect(os.WriteFile(taskPath, []byte(taskContent), 0o600)).To(Succeed())\n    _, err := agent.Run(context.Background(), domain.TaskPhase(entryPhase), taskContent, factory.CreateFileResultDeliverer(taskPath))\n    ...\n}\n```\n\nWait — the agent.Run's phase argument should be the entry phase (planning for most, ai_review for j). The deliverer reads the file from taskPath (we wrote it). But note agent.Run parses taskContent, and deliverer reads the original from disk. Both must match. Fine.\n\nAlso need `domain` import for TaskPhase.\n\nHmm, but GinkgoT().TempDir() is available in Ginkgo v2. Yes, `GinkgoT()` returns testing.TB. Use `GinkgoT().TempDir()`.\n\nClone fixture: `<tmp>/repos/bborbe/foo/pkg/x/y.go` with 3 lines. cloneRoot = filepath.Join(tmp, \"repos\"). Good.\n\nNote: agent dir is tmp; the deliverer writes taskPath in a separate temp dir. Good.\n\nThen read file:\n```go\ndata, err := os.ReadFile(taskPath)\nExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\nreturn string(data), fake\n```\n\nNow assertions helpers:\n\n```go\nfunc frontmatterValue(content, key string) string {\n    fm, _ := delivery.ParseMarkdownFrontmatter(content)\n    v, _ := fm[key].(string)\n    return v\n}\nfunc countLinesWithPrefix(content, prefix string) int\nfunc containsSection? Use strings.Contains(content, \"\\n## Plan\\n\") maybe.\n```\n\nOrder of ## Plan, ## Verdict, ## Review: use strings.Index.\n\nAbsence of ## Verdict: countLinesWithPrefix(content, \"## Verdict\") == 0.\n\nNote: `delivery.ParseMarkdownFrontmatter` returns map[string]any and body. Exported. Good.\n\nNow the ten cases. I'll implement as DescribeTable? The requirement says \"Implement each as its own spec (a DescribeTable over a case struct is fine, as long as each row asserts the whole list)\". A table with a function per row is complex given different assertions. I'll write individual `It`s calling shared helpers, to keep each clear. `dupl` may complain about duplicated blocks; but each has different assertions. Fine.\n\nLet me carefully compute each case's fake responses and task fixture.\n\nCase (a): entry planning. responses:\n0: done plan\n1: done verdict High valid line 3\n2: done review passing\nTask body includes stale ## Failure.\nAssert: status completed, phase done, ## Plan/Verdict/Review order, no ## Failure.\n\nCase (b): entry planning. responses:\n0: plan\n1: verdict Medium valid line 3\nNo third response (should not be called). Assert assignee \"\", phase execution, ## Failure contains \"below High\", ## Verdict present, ## Review absent, RunCallCount == 2, prompt[1] contains scripts/prometheus-query.sh.\n\nNote: With Medium, gate rule j: line guard passes, returns needs_input. Good.\n\nCase (c): entry planning. responses:\n0: plan\n1: verdict High line 999\n2: review passing (ai_review runs)\nAssert assignee \"\", phase ai_review, ## Failure contains \"beyond end of file\", \"3\", and each evidence line prefixed \"> \". No ## Verdict. status not completed.\n\nWait: evidence contains two lines: `scripts/prometheus-query.sh '...'` and `{\"status\":\"success\"}`. The failure message is `> \"pkg/x/y.go:999\" beyond end of file (3 lines); evidence:` then `> scripts/...` then `> {\"status\":\"success\"}`. So assert `> ` + each evidence line. Good.\n\nCase (d): entry planning. responses:\n0: plan\n1: verdict High but defect_id: defect-2\nAssert 