ure contains \"below High\".\n\nNote: for entry at ai_review, `## Plan` absent. That's fine.\n\nNow important detail for (j): the fake runner gets only one call (review). RunReturnsOnCall(0, review). Good.\n\nNow, in cases where the task file starts at phase planning, the first delivery from planning writes the file. But wait: `Agent.Run` reads taskContent param and parses it into md. The deliverer reads the file. They match because we write same content. Good.\n\nAnother subtlety: The passthrough generator ignores originalContent and uses result.Output. On planning done, result.Output is marshaled md including the task frontmatter. The wrapper recordPhase set phase=planning (already). applyStatusFrontmatter sets phase=execution. File written. Good.\n\nNow, the `defect_id` in the task frontmatter must survive marshaling. Yes.\n\nNow, case (a) stale ## Failure: planning ShouldRun: ## Plan absent → run. Execution ShouldRun: ## Verdict absent → run. But note `failureMarked` in agentStep: the md has ## Failure; ShouldRun returns true regardless. For ai_review: ## Review absent → true. At the end wrapper removes ## Failure. Good.\n\nBut wait — there's a subtle issue: in case (a), when planning step writes ## Plan, the stale ## Failure remains. Then execution writes ## Verdict. Then ai_review writes ## Review. gate.Review passes → removeSection(md, \"## Failure\"). Then result Done NextPhase=done. Marshal. Delivery writes no ## Failure. Good.\n\nNow — the task file content in (a) initial has ## Failure after ## Observation. Does the agentlib Markdown parser treat the ## Failure body correctly? Yes.\n\nNow let me double check the `parseFileLine` and line guard: repo \"bborbe/foo\" joined with cloneRoot. We write fixture at `<tmp>/repos/bborbe/foo/pkg/x/y.go`. cloneRoot = `<tmp>/repos`. repoRoot = `<tmp>/repos/bborbe/foo`. target = .../pkg/x/y.go. EvalSymlinks works (temp dirs on linux may be /tmp symlink? EvalSymlinks resolves; within check compares resolvedRepoRoot and re