ckage `factory_test` — can reuse! Since both files are package factory_test, doneResult is shared). Good, but I'll define needsInputResult/failedResult here.\n\nCareful: function name collisions across files in same package. `doneResult` defined in dispatch file; use it in phase_chain too.\n\nAssertion helpers:\n\n```go\nfunc fmField(content, key string) string {\n    fm, _ := delivery.ParseMarkdownFrontmatter(content)\n    v, _ := fm[key].(string)\n    return v\n}\nfunc countHeading(content, heading string) int {\n    n := 0\n    for _, line := range strings.Split(content, \"\\n\") {\n        if strings.HasPrefix(line, heading) { n++ }\n    }\n    return n\n}\nfunc failureBody(content string) string {\n    md, err := agentlib.ParseMarkdown(context.Background(), content)\n    Expect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n    section, ok := md.FindSection(\"## Failure\")\n    if !ok { return \"\" }\n    return section.Body\n}\nfunc assertSectionOrder(content string, headings ...string) {\n    prev := -1\n    for _, h := range headings {\n        idx := strings.Index(content, \"\\n\"+h+\"\\n\")\n        Expect(idx).To(BeNumerically(\">\", prev), \"section %q out of order\", h)\n        prev = idx\n    }\n}\n```\n\nWait: headings at start of body may be preceded by \"\\n\". The first section after frontmatter: \"---\\n\\n## Observation\". Fine.\n\nActually `strings.Index(content, \"\\n\"+h+\"\\n\")` works if headings have blank line after. Marsha may produce \"## Plan\\n\\nbody\". Yes.\n\nBut if heading is the first line after frontmatter? Not for Plan. Fine. Use `\"\\n\"+h`.\n\nBetter: find index of line equal to h:\n```go\nfunc sectionIndex(content, heading string) int {\n    offset := 0\n    for _, line := range strings.SplitAfter(content, \"\\n\") {\n        if strings.TrimRight(line, \"\\n\") == heading { return offset }\n        offset += len(line)\n    }\n    return -1\n}\n```\nThis is robust. Then order via indices.\n\nNow the cases.\n\nPlan output helper:\n```go\nfunc pl