ason:**\\n\\n```\\nstale attempt\\n```\\n\"\n```\nPlaced after ## Observation.\n\nNow assertions per case.\n\n(a):\n- result.Status Done\n- fm status completed, phase done, assignee? On completed, assignee preserved? applyStatusFrontmatter Done+done doesn't touch assignee, so assignee remains \"defect-diagnoser-agent\". Requirement only asserts status, phase, sections, no failure. Fine.\n- section order Plan, Verdict, Review\n- countHeading(\"## Failure\") == 0\n- countHeading(\"## Verdict\") == 1\n\n(b):\n- fm assignee == \"\", phase == execution\n- failure body contains \"below High\"\n- countHeading Verdict == 1, Review == 0\n- fake.RunCallCount() == 2\n- prompt[1] contains \"scripts/prometheus-query.sh\"\n\n(c):\n- fm assignee \"\", phase ai_review, status != completed\n- failure body contains \"beyond end of file\", \"3\"\n- each evidence line: failure body contains \"> \" + line\n- countHeading Verdict == 0\n\nWait: evidence has 2 lines. failureBody from parsed md — ParseMarkdown will parse the ## Failure section body which includes \"```\\n> ...\\n> ...\\n```\". Does the parser include fence content? It splits by headings only; the body is everything until next heading. So yes contains. Good.\n\nBut note: `failureBody` parsed via agentlib.ParseMarkdown. The written content's ## Failure section body: \"> ...\". Good.\n\nAlso assert status != \"completed\": fmField(content,\"status\") != \"completed\".\n\n(d):\n- assignee \"\", phase execution, countHeading Verdict == 0\n- fake.RunCallCount() == 2\n\n(e):\n- phase execution, assignee \"defect-diagnoser-agent\", countHeading Failure == 1, Verdict == 0\n\n(f):\n- phase execution, assignee \"\"\n\n(g):\n- result.Status Failed, result.Message contains \"## Plan\"\n- RunCallCount == 1\n- phase planning\n- countHeading Plan == 0, Verdict == 0\n- failureBody has no line with prefix \"#\"\n\n(h):\n- result.Status Failed, message contains \"## Verdict\"\n- phase execution\n- countHeading Verdict == 0\n\n(i):\n- result.Status Failed, message contains \"## Review\"\n- phase ai_review\n- countHeading Review == 0, Verdict == 1\n\n(j):\n- status != completed\n- assignee \"\", phase ai_review\n- failure contains \"below High\"\n\nNow, one concern for case (g): result.Message — the wrapper's prefixedResult prefixes lines with \"> \". `heading rule: section \"## Plan\" contains a column-0 heading line`. Contains \"## Plan\". Good.\n\nAnother concern: For (g), `RunCallCount == 1` — planning is the only call; failed exits. Good.\n\nFor (h), count Verdict == 0: execution step wrote ## Verdict then checkHeading removed it. But the execution result is failed, so no ai_review. Good.\n\nFor (i): execution wrote valid verdict (kept), advanced to ai_review, ai_review failed & removed ## Review. Count Verdict == 1. Good.\n\nNow, a subtle issue in case (h): the execution output is `verdictBlock + \"## Verdict\\nforged\\n\"`. The inner step writes this as the body of ## Verdict. Then wrapper checkHeading scans body. But `lastYAMLBlock` would parse the block fine; however checkHeading runs first → failed. Good.\n\nNow, a critical concern about `## Failure` body parsing for the \"no line starting with #\" assertion in (g). The passthrough generator's buildFailureSection:\n```\n## Failure\n\n- **Reason:**\n\n```\n> heading rule: section \"## Plan\" contains a column-0 heading line\n```\n```\nWait — `buildFailureSection` writes \"```\\n\" + message + \"\\n```\\n\". The message is \"> heading rule...\" (prefixed). So the section body has lines \"- **Reason:**\", \"\", \"```\", \"> ...\", \"```\". None start with \"#\". Good.\n\nBut wait: the written file's ## Failure section is appended by ReplaceOrAppendSection. The section heading \"## Failure\" then body. Parsing gives body without the heading. Good.\n\nNow: there's an important subtlety about how `ReplaceOrAppendSection` works with result.Output that already contains ## Failure. For case (a) stale failure, on final success the wrapper removes ## Failure from md before marshal, so output has none. Good.\n\nBut for failed/needs_input cases, passthrough does ReplaceOrAppendSection(updated, \"## Failure\", buildFailureSection(result)). `updated` is result.Output (marshaled md) which does not contain ## Failure (for our tasks without stale). So appends. Good.\n\nNow, case (b): phase execution, but the original task's ## Plan exists. fine.\n\nLet me also double-check: For needs_input/failed, `applyStatusFrontmatter` is applied to result.Output which is marshaled md. The md includes frontmatter from parse. Does `md.Marshal` preserve all frontmatter fields (task_type, trigger_count, max_triggers)? Need to verify Markdown.Marshal. Let me check agent_markdown.go.","signature":"llm-proxy"}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65223de2-d5ca-493e-b6ca-024741641a7c","uuid":"598659f5-c622-4ec9-96b8-4131ca3178ca","timestamp":"2026-11-26T19:05:55.805Z"}
