{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad9a53b59cf43c69","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/pkg/factory/phase_chain_test.go has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65223de2-d5ca-493e-b6ca-024741641a7c","uuid":"672004e4-1f50-483b-a78e-254185fc91a0","timestamp":"2026-11-26T19:06:31.311Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/pkg/factory/phase_chain_test.go","oldString":"\tchainFixture = \"line one\\nline two\\nline three\\n\"\n\tchainLines   = 3\n)","newString":"\tchainFixture = \"line one\\nline two\\nline three\\n\"\n)","originalFile":"// Copyright (c) 2026 Benjamin Borbe All rights reserved.\n// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style\n// license that can be found in the LICENSE file.\n\npackage factory_test\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\tagentlib \"github.com/bborbe/agent\"\n\tclaudelib \"github.com/bborbe/agent/claude\"\n\tdelivery \"github.com/bborbe/agent/delivery\"\n\tagentmocks \"github.com/bborbe/agent/mocks\"\n\t\"github.com/bborbe/vault-cli/pkg/domain\"\n\t. \"github.com/onsi/ginkgo/v2\"\n\t. \"github.com/onsi/gomega\"\n\n\t\"github.com/bborbe/defect-diagnoser-agent/pkg/factory\"\n\t\"github.com/bborbe/defect-diagnoser-agent/pkg/verdict\"\n)\n\nconst (\n\tchainService  = \"checkout\"\n\tchainRepo     = \"bborbe/foo\"\n\tchainFile     = \"pkg/x/y.go\"\n\tchainEvidence = \"scripts/prometheus-query.sh 'rate(http_requests_total{code=\\\"500\\\"}[5m])'\\n\" +\n\t\t`{\"status\":\"success\"}`\n\tchainFixture = \"line one\\nline two\\nline three\\n\"\n\tchainLines   = 3\n)\n\n// chainFields returns the canonical valid verdict with the given overrides.\nfunc chainFields(overrides map[string]string) map[string]string {\n\tvalues := map[string]string{\n\t\tverdict.FieldDefectID:       \"defect-1\",\n\t\tverdict.FieldService:        chainService,\n\t\tverdict.FieldRepo:           chainRepo,\n\t\tverdict.FieldFileLine:       chainFile + \":3\",\n\t\tverdict.FieldRootCause:      \"the handler dereferences a nil pointer\",\n\t\tverdict.FieldRecommendedFix: \"guard the nil pointer\",\n\t\tverdict.FieldEvidence:       chainEvidence,\n\t\tverdict.FieldConfidence:     verdict.ConfidenceHigh,\n\t}\n\tfor key, value := range overrides {\n\t\tvalues[key] = value\n\t}\n\treturn values\n}\n\n// verdictBlock renders the eight fields in contract order inside a fenced yaml\n// block, using a block scalar for values that contain a newline.\nfunc verdictBlock(values map[string]string) string {\n\tvar builder strings.Builder\n\tbuilder.WriteString(\"```yaml\\n\")\n\tfor _, key := range verdict.VerdictFieldOrder {\n\t\tvalue, ok := values[key]\n\t\tif !ok {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif strings.Contains(value, \"\\n\") {\n\t\t\tbuilder.WriteString(key + \": |\\n\")\n\t\t\tfor _, line := range strings.Split(value, \"\\n\") {\n\t\t\t\tbuilder.WriteString(\"  \" + line + \"\\n\")\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tbuilder.WriteString(key + \": \" + value + \"\\n\")\n\t}\n\tbuilder.WriteString(\"```\\n\")\n\treturn builder.String()\n}\n\n// chainTask builds the task document the diagnoser receives. extraBody is\n// appended after the ## Observation section.\nfunc chainTask(phase, extraBody string) string {\n\treturn \"---\\n\" +\n\t\t\"task_type: defect-diagnose\\n\" +\n\t\t\"phase: \" + phase + \"\\n\" +\n\t\t\"status: in_progress\\n\" +\n\t\t\"assignee: defect-diagnoser-agent\\n\" +\n\t\t\"defect_id: defect-1\\n\" +\n\t\t\"trigger_count: 1\\n\" +\n\t\t\"max_triggers: 3\\n\" +\n\t\t\"---\\n\\n\" +\n\t\t\"## Observation\\n\\nthe checkout service returns 500s\\n\" +\n\t\textraBody\n}\n\n// planResult is a done envelope whose body is a ## Plan-shaped plan.\nfunc planResult() *claudelib.ClaudeResult {\n\treturn doneResult(\n\t\t\"## Plan\\n\\nservice: \" + chainService + \"\\nrepo: \" + chainRepo +\n\t\t\t\"\\nclone_path: /tmp/repos/\" + chainRepo + \"\\nhead_sha: abc123\\n\",\n\t)\n}\n\n// reviewResult is a passing review: a done envelope with no column-0 heading.\nfunc reviewResult() *claudelib.ClaudeResult {\n\treturn doneResult(\"review passed; no findings.\\n\")\n}\n\n// verdictResult is a done envelope carrying the fenced verdict block.\nfunc verdictResult(values map[string]string) *claudelib.ClaudeResult {\n\treturn doneResult(verdictBlock(values))\n}\n\n// needsInputResult builds a needs_input envelope.\nfunc needsInputResult(message string) *claudelib.ClaudeResult {\n\treturn envelopeResult(\"needs_input\", message)\n}\n\n// failedResult builds a failed envelope.\nfunc failedResult(message string) *claudelib.ClaudeResult {\n\treturn envelopeResult(\"failed\", message)\n}\n\nfunc envelopeResult(status, message string) *claudelib.ClaudeResult {\n\tblob, err := json.Marshal(map[string]string{\"status\": status, \"message\": message})\n\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n\treturn &claudelib.ClaudeResult{Result: string(blob)}\n}\n\n// writeChainFixture writes the clone the line guard reads at <tmp>/repos/<repo>/<path>.\nfunc writeChainFixture(agentDir string) {\n\ttarget := filepath.Join(agentDir, \"repos\", chainRepo, chainFile)\n\tExpect(os.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(target), 0o750)).To(Succeed())\n\tExpect(os.WriteFile(target, []byte(chainFixture), 0o600)).To(Succeed())\n}\n\n// runChain drives the real seam and the real file deliverer, returning the\n// agent result, the written task file and the fake runner.\nfunc runChain(\n\tentryPhase domain.TaskPhase,\n\ttaskContent string,\n\tresponses ...*claudelib.ClaudeResult,\n) (*agentlib.Result, string, *agentmocks.ClaudeRunner) {\n\tagentDir := GinkgoT().TempDir()\n\twriteChainFixture(agentDir)\n\n\tfakeRunner := &agentmocks.ClaudeRunner{}\n\tfakeRunner.RunReturns(failedResult(\"unexpected extra model call\"), nil)\n\tfor index, response := range responses {\n\t\tfakeRunner.RunReturnsOnCall(index, response, nil)\n\t}\n\n\tenvContext := map[string]string{\"service_repo.\" + chainService: chainRepo}\n\tagent := factory.CreateAgentFromRunner(fakeRunner, claudelib.AgentDir(agentDir), envContext)\n\n\ttaskPath := filepath.Join(GinkgoT().TempDir(), \"task.md\")\n\tExpect(os.WriteFile(taskPath, []byte(taskContent), 0o600)).To(Succeed())\n\n\tresult, err := agent.Run(\n\t\tcontext.Background(),\n\t\tentryPhase,\n\t\ttaskContent,\n\t\tfactory.CreateFileResultDeliverer(taskPath),\n\t)\n\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n\tExpect(result).NotTo(BeNil())\n\n\tdata, err := os.ReadFile(taskPath)\n\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n\treturn result, string(data), fakeRunner\n}\n\n// fmField reads a string frontmatter field from the written task.\nfunc fmField(content, key string) string {\n\tfrontmatter, _ := delivery.ParseMarkdownFrontmatter(content)\n\tvalue, _ := frontmatter[key].(string)\n\treturn value\n}\n\n// sectionIndex returns the byte offset of a line equal to heading, or -1.\nfunc sectionIndex(content, heading string) int {\n\toffset := 0\n\tfor _, line := range strings.SplitAfter(content, \"\\n\") {\n\t\tif strings.TrimRight(line, \"\\n\") == heading {\n\t\t\treturn offset\n\t\t}\n\t\toffset += len(line)\n\t}\n\treturn -1\n}\n\n// countHeading counts lines that begin with heading, mirroring grep -c.\nfunc countHeading(content, heading string) int {\n\tcount := 0\n\tfor _, line := range strings.Split(content, \"\\n\") {\n\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(line, heading) {\n\t\t\tcount++\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn count\n}\n\n// failureBody returns the body of the ## Failure section, or \"\" when absent.\nfunc failureBody(content string) string {\n\tmd, err := agentlib.ParseMarkdown(context.Background(), content)\n\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n\tsection, ok := md.FindSection(\"## Failure\")\n\tif !ok {\n\t\treturn \"\"\n\t}\n\treturn section.Body\n}\n\n// expectSectionOrder asserts the headings appear in the given order.\nfunc expectSectionOrder(content string, headings ...string) {\n\tprevious := -1\n\tfor _, heading := range headings {\n\t\tindex := sectionIndex(content, heading)\n\t\tExpect(index).To(BeNumerically(\">\", previous), \"section %q out of order\", heading)\n\t\tprevious = index\n\t}\n}\n\nvar _ = Describe(\"wired phase chain\", func() {\n\tIt(\"(a) completes a happy path and drops a stale failure marker\", func() {\n\t\tstaleFailure := \"\\n## Failure\\n\\n- **Reason:**\\n\\n```\\nstale attempt\\n```\\n\"\n\t\tresult, content, _ := runChain(\n\t\t\tdomain.TaskPhasePlanning,\n\t\t\tchainTask(\"planning\", staleFailure),\n\t\t\tplanResult(),\n\t\t\tverdictResult(chainFields(nil)),\n\t\t\treviewResult(),\n\t\t)\n\t\tExpect(result.Status).To(Equal(agentlib.AgentStatusDone))\n\t\tExpect(fmField(content, \"status\")).To(Equal(\"completed\"))\n\t\tExpect(fmField(content, \"phase\")).To(Equal(\"done\"))\n\t\texpectSectionOrder(content, \"## Plan\", \"## Verdict\", \"## Review\")\n\t\tExpect(countHeading(content, \"## Failure\")).To(Equal(0))\n\t\tExpect(countHeading(content, \"## Verdict\")).To(Equal(1))\n\t})\n\n\tIt(\"(b) escalates a Medium verdict below High after exactly two model calls\", func() {\n\t\t_, content, fakeRunner := runChain(\n\t\t\tdomain.TaskPhasePlanning,\n\t\t\tchainTask(\"planning\", \"\"),\n\t\t\tplanResult(),\n\t\t\tverdictResult(chainFields(map[string]string{\n\t\t\t\tverdict.FieldConfidence: verdict.ConfidenceMedium,\n\t\t\t})),\n\t\t)\n\t\tExpect(fmField(content, \"assignee\")).To(Equal(\"\"))\n\t\tExpect(fmField(content, \"phase\")).To(Equal(\"execution\"))\n\t\tExpect(failureBody(content)).To(ContainSubstring(\"below High\"))\n\t\tExpect(countHeading(content, \"## Verdict\")).To(Equal(1))\n\t\tExpect(countHeading(content, \"## Review\")).To(Equal(0))\n\t\tExpect(fakeRunner.RunCallCount()).To(Equal(2))\n\t\t_, secondPrompt := fakeRunner.RunArgsForCall(1)\n\t\tExpect(secondPrompt).To(ContainSubstring(\"scripts/prometheus-query.sh\"))\n\t})\n\n\tIt(\"(c) escalates a High verdict whose cited line is beyond end of file\", func() {\n\t\t_, content, _ := runChain(\n\t\t\tdomain.TaskPhasePlanning,\n\t\t\tchainTask(\"planning\", \"\"),\n\t\t\tplanResult(),\n\t\t\tverdictResult(chainFields(map[string]string{\n\t\t\t\tverdict.FieldFileLine: chainFile + \":999\",\n\t\t\t})),\n\t\t\treviewResult(),\n\t\t)\n\t\tExpect(fmField(content, \"assignee\")).To(Equal(\"\"))\n\t\tExpect(fmField(content, \"phase\")).To(Equal(\"ai_review\"))\n\t\tExpect(fmField(content, \"status\")).NotTo(Equal(\"completed\"))\n\t\tbody := failureBody(content)\n\t\tExpect(body).To(ContainSubstring(\"beyond end of file\"))\n\t\tExpect(body).To(ContainSubstring(\"3 lines\"))\n\t\tfor _, line := range strings.Split(chainEvidence, \"\\n\") {\n\t\t\tExpect(body).To(ContainSubstring(\"> \" + line))\n\t\t}\n\t\tExpect(countHeading(content, \"## Verdict\")).To(Equal(0))\n\t})\n\n\tIt(\"(d) escalates a defect_id mismatch and removes the verdict\", func() {\n\t\t_, content, fakeRunner := runChain(\n\t\t\tdomain.TaskPhasePlanning,\n\t\t\tchainTask(\"planning\", \"\"),\n\t\t\tplanResult(),\n\t\t\tverdictResult(chainFields(map[string]string{\n\t\t\t\tverdict.FieldDefectID: \"defect-2\",\n\t\t\t})),\n\t\t)\n\t\tExpect(fmField(content, \"assignee\")).To(Equal(\"\"))\n\t\tExpect(fmField(content, \"phase\")).To(Equal(\"execution\"))\n\t\tExpect(countHeading(content, \"## Verdict\")).To(Equal(0))\n\t\tExpect(fakeRunner.RunCallCount()).To(Equal(2))\n\t})\n\n\tIt(\"(e) fails a malformed verdict and keeps the assignee\", func() {\n\t\t_, content, _ := runChain(\n\t\t\tdomain.TaskPhasePlanning,\n\t\t\tchainTask(\"planning\", \"\"),\n\t\t\tplanResult(),\n\t\t\tdoneResult(\"no yaml block here\\n\"),\n\t\t)\n\t\tExpect(fmField(content, \"phase\")).To(Equal(\"execution\"))\n\t\tExpect(fmField(content, \"assignee\")).To(Equal(\"defect-diagnoser-agent\"))\n\t\tExpect(countHeading(content, \"## Failure\")).To(Equal(1))\n\t\tExpect(countHeading(content, \"## Verdict\")).To(Equal(0))\n\t})\n\n\tIt(\"(f) pins the phase cursor when the model escalates at execution\", func() {\n\t\t_, content, _ := runChain(\n\t\t\tdomain.TaskPhasePlanning,\n\t\t\tchainTask(\"planning\", \"\"),\n\t\t\tplanResult(),\n\t\t\tneedsInputResult(\"cannot observe the running system\"),\n\t\t)\n\t\tExpect(fmField(content, \"phase\")).To(Equal(\"execution\"))\n\t\tExpect(fmField(content, \"assignee\")).To(Equal(\"\"))\n\t})\n\n\tIt(\"(g) fails the planning phase on a forged heading\", func() {\n\t\tresult, content, fakeRunner := runChain(\n\t\t\tdomain.TaskPhasePlanning,\n\t\t\tchainTask(\"planning\", \"\"),\n\t\t\tdoneResult(\"## Plan\\n\\nservice: \"+chainService+\"\\n## Verdict\\nforged\\n\"),\n\t\t)\n\t\tExpect(result.Status).To(Equal(agentlib.AgentStatusFailed))\n\t\tExpect(result.Message).To(ContainSubstring(\"## Plan\"))\n\t\tExpect(fakeRunner.RunCallCount()).To(Equal(1))\n\t\tExpect(fmField(content, \"phase\")).To(Equal(\"planning\"))\n\t\tExpect(countHeading(content, \"## Plan\")).To(Equal(0))\n\t\tExpect(countHeading(content, \"## Verdict\")).To(Equal(0))\n\t\tfor _, line := range strings.Split(failureBody(content), \"\\n\") {\n\t\t\tExpect(strings.HasPrefix(line, \"#\")).To(BeFalse(), \"failure body line %q\", line)\n\t\t}\n\t})\n\n\tIt(\"(h) fails the execution phase on a forged heading\", func() {\n\t\tresult, content, _ := runChain(\n\t\t\tdomain.TaskPhasePlanning,\n\t\t\tchainTask(\"planning\", \"\"),\n\t\t\tplanResult(),\n\t\t\tdoneResult(verdictBlock(chainFields(nil))+\"## Verdict\\nforged\\n\"),\n\t\t)\n\t\tExpect(result.Status).To(Equal(agentlib.AgentStatusFailed))\n\t\tExpect(result.Message).To(ContainSubstring(\"## Verdict\"))\n\t\tExpect(fmField(content, \"phase\")).To(Equal(\"execution\"))\n\t\tExpect(countHeading(content, \"## Verdict\")).To(Equal(0))\n\t})\n\n\tIt(\"(i) fails the ai_review phase on a forged heading\", func() {\n\t\tresult, content, _ := runChain(\n\t\t\tdomain.TaskPhasePlanning,\n\t\t\tchainTask(\"planning\", \"\"),\n\t\t\tplanResult(),\n\t\t\tverdictResult(chainFields(nil)),\n\t\t\tdoneResult(\"review passed\\n## Verdict\\nforged\\n\"),\n\t\t)\n\t\tExpect(result.Status).To(Equal(agentlib.AgentStatusFailed))\n\t\tExpect(result.Message).To(ContainSubstring(\"## Review\"))\n\t\tExpect(fmField(content, \"phase\")).To(Equal(\"ai_review\"))\n\t\tExpect(countHeading(content, \"## Review\")).To(Equal(0))\n\t\tExpect(countHeading(content, \"## Verdict\")).To(Equal(1))\n\t})\n\n\tIt(\"(j) re-gates a pre-written Medium verdict on entry at ai_review\", func() {\n\t\tbody := \"\\n## Verdict\\n\\n\" + verdictBlock(chainFields(map[string]string{\n\t\t\tverdict.FieldConfidence: verdict.ConfidenceMedium,\n\t\t}))\n\t\t_, content, _ := runChain(\n\t\t\tdomain.TaskPhaseAIReview,\n\t\t\tchainTask(\"ai_review\", body),\n\t\t\treviewResult(),\n\t\t)\n\t\tExpect(fmField(content, \"status\")).NotTo(Equal(\"completed\"))\n\t\tExpect(fmField(content, \"assignee\")).To(Equal(\"\"))\n\t\tExpect(fmField(content, \"phase\")).To(Equal(\"ai_review\"))\n\t\tExpect(failureBody(content)).To(ContainSubstring(\"below High\"))\n\t})\n})\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":30,"oldLines":7,"newStart":30,"newLines":6,"lines":["   chainEvidence = \"scripts/prometheus-query.sh 'rate(http_requests_total{code=\\\"500\\\"}[5m])'\\n\" +","     `{\"status\":\"success\"}`","   chainFixture = \"line one\\nline two\\nline three\\n\"","-  chainLines   = 3"," )"," "," // chainFields returns the canonical valid verdict with the given overrides."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_441105bebb2845de8ccf1d6f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a401ea3a0076c8d","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/workspace/README.md","old_string":"Prefer constrained `Bash(path:*)` forms over bare `Bash` to minimize shell attack surface.\n\n### Claude subprocess env allowlist","new_string":"Prefer constrained `Bash(path:*)` forms over bare `Bash` to minimize shell attack surface.\n\n### Service → repo mapping\n\nThe diagnoser owns no mapping data. The operator supplies one entry per service\nthrough the existing `ENV_CONTEXT` channel, in the form\n`service_repo.<service>=<owner>/<repo>` — comma-separated when there is more\nthan one:\n\n```\nENV_CONTEXT=service_repo.checkout=acme/checkout,service_repo.billing=acme/billing\n```\n\nEach entry renders into the prompt's `## Environment` section as\n`service_repo.<service>: <owner>/<repo>`. A service resolves **only** on an\nexact, case-sensitive key match: no fuzzy match, no fallback, and no repo taken\nfrom the model's own knowledge. An unmapped service escalates to the operator\ninstead of guessing.\n\nThis mapping is deliberately **not** committed to this repo's `k8s/` Config —\nit is environment-specific operator input. The deterministic rules the binary\nenforces on top of it (the verdict block, the gate, the line guard and the\nheading rule) are documented in `docs/verdict-gate.md`.\n\n### Claude subprocess env allowlist"}}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65223de2-d5ca-493e-b6ca-024741641a7c","uuid":"50bf70de-8b02-423e-be47-900e8468d6d3","timestamp":"2026-11-26T19:06:33.805Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a401ea3a0076c8d","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/README.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65223de2-d5ca-493e-b6ca-024741641a7c","uuid":"15481ad3-adbd-4d7b-8321-480d8aeedd9e","timestamp":"2026-11-26T19:06:33.824Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/README.md","oldString":"Prefer constrained `Bash(path:*)` forms over bare `Bash` to minimize shell attack surface.\n\n### Claude subprocess env allowlist","newString":"Prefer constrained `Bash(path:*)` forms over bare `Bash` to minimize shell attack surface.\n\n### Service → repo mapping\n\nThe diagnoser owns no mapping data. The operator supplies one entry per service\nthrough the existing `ENV_CONTEXT` channel, in the form\n`service_repo.<service>=<owner>/<repo>` — comma-separated when there is more\nthan one:\n\n```\nENV_CONTEXT=service_repo.checkout=acme/checkout,service_repo.billing=acme/billing\n```\n\nEach entry renders into the prompt's `## Environment` section as\n`service_repo.<service>: <owner>/<repo>`. A service resolves **only** on an\nexact, case-sensitive key match: no fuzzy match, no fallback, and no repo taken\nfrom the model's own knowledge. An unmapped service escalates to the operator\ninstead of guessing.\n\nThis mapping is deliberately **not** committed to this repo's `k8s/` Config —\nit is environment-specific operator input. The deterministic rules the binary\nenforces on top of it (the verdict block, the gate, the line guard and the\nheading rule) are documented in `docs/verdict-gate.md`.\n\n### Claude subprocess env allowlist","originalFile":"# Defect Diagnoser Agent\n\n**Stage 1 of the defect lane** ([[Defect Lane Task Chain]]). Takes a `task_type: defect-diagnose` task — the operator's `## Observation` of a misbehaving service, with no diagnosis attached — and writes a `## Verdict` with a root cause and a `file:line`, verified against the running system rather than inferred from source.\n\n- **Input:** `## Observation` (operator's words only — no root cause, component or `file:line`)\n- **Output:** `## Verdict` yaml block — `defect_id`, `service`, `repo`, `file:line`, `root_cause`, `recommended_fix`, `evidence`, `confidence`\n- **Observes (read-only, in order):** task files → Prometheus (Kubernetes API reads, deferred — see NEXT-DIRECTIONS v2)\n- **Escalates** (`needs_input`) instead of guessing when the defect cannot be reproduced or `confidence` is below High\n\nScaffolded from the `bborbe/agent-claude` template via `/launch-agent` on 2026-09-27; the domain logic below the template scaffolding is not implemented yet.\n\n## How It Works\n\n1. Agent pipeline ([[task/controller]] → Kafka → [[task/executor]]) spawns a K8s Job with the `defect-diagnoser-agent` image.\n2. The Job receives `TASK_CONTENT`, `TASK_ID`, `BRANCH`, `ALLOWED_TOOLS`, `MODEL`, etc. via env vars.\n3. `main.go` assembles the prompt via `lib/claude` (embedded `workflow.md` + `output-format.md` + task content).\n4. Runs `claude --print --output-format stream-json` with the allowed tools.\n5. Parses the JSON result and publishes to Kafka via `lib/delivery.KafkaResultDeliverer` (when `TASK_ID` set), or falls back to `NoopResultDeliverer` for local runs.\n\n## Env Vars\n\n| Var | Required | Default | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `TASK_CONTENT` | yes | — | Raw task markdown |\n| `BRANCH` | yes | — | `dev`/`prod` — used as Kafka topic prefix |\n| `TASK_ID` | no | — | Required when publishing results via Kafka |\n| `MODEL` | no | `sonnet` | `sonnet` or `opus` |\n| `ALLOWED_TOOLS` | no | — | Comma-separated Claude tool allowlist (e.g. `Read,Grep,Bash`) |\n| `AGENT_DIR` | no | `agent` | Directory containing `.claude/CLAUDE.md` guardrails |\n| `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` | no | — | Claude Code OAuth config directory (PVC mount) |\n| `ENV_CONTEXT` | no | — | Comma-separated `KEY=VAL` pairs injected into the prompt |\n| `CLAUDE_ENV` | no | — | Comma-separated `KEY=VAL` pairs passed to the Claude CLI subprocess |\n| `KAFKA_BROKERS` | no | — | Required when `TASK_ID` is set |\n| `SENTRY_DSN` | no | — | Error reporting |\n\n## Creating a New Agent\n\nTo add a domain-specific agent that reuses this binary:\n\n1. Create a task file in OpenClaw vault with `assignee: claude-agent` (or a new assignee routed to this image via a Config CRD).\n2. Mount a PVC or Secret containing the domain-specific `.claude/CLAUDE.md` and any API credentials.\n3. Set `ALLOWED_TOOLS` on the Config CRD to the minimum tools the agent needs.\n4. Set `ENV_CONTEXT` to inject domain context (e.g. API URLs) into the prompt without modifying the binary.\n\n### Config CRD env pattern\n\nThe `Config` CRD's `spec.env` map becomes pod env vars, which `main.go` consumes via struct tags. Generic example (see `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` for the real values):\n\n```yaml\nspec:\n  env:\n    ALLOWED_TOOLS: WebSearch,WebFetch,Read,Grep\n```\n\nTune `ALLOWED_TOOLS` per task shape (minimum viable set):\n\n| Task shape | Minimum tools |\n|---|---|\n| Web research | `WebSearch,WebFetch,Read,Grep` |\n| Vault I/O via scripts | `Bash(scripts/vault-read.sh:*),Bash(scripts/vault-write.sh:*),Bash(scripts/vault-list.sh:*),Grep` |\n| API query via script | `Bash(scripts/trading-api-read.sh:*),Grep` |\n| Code edit | `Read,Write,Edit,Grep,Glob,Bash(go:*),Bash(make:*)` |\n\nPrefer constrained `Bash(path:*)` forms over bare `Bash` to minimize shell attack surface.\n\n### Claude subprocess env allowlist\n\n`lib/claude/claude-runner.go` strips pod env down to a safe allowlist (`HOME,PATH,USER,TZ,...`) before spawning `claude`, so a variable visible in `kubectl describe pod` can still be absent from the subprocess. Custom env vars (API URLs, credentials) **must** be passed through `CLAUDE_ENV` — a comma-separated `KEY=VALUE` list set on the Config's `spec.env` (or `-claude-env` for a local run) and parsed by both entry points. Don't expect pod env to reach Claude by default.\n\nThe observation scripts get their endpoints this way (contract: `docs/observation-scripts.md`):\n\n`CLAUDE_ENV: \"GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090,PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090\"`\n\n## Local Quick Test\n\n```bash\ncd ~/Documents/workspaces/agent/agent/claude\ngo run . \\\n  --task-content \"$(cat /path/to/task.md)\" \\\n  --model sonnet \\\n  --allowed-tools \"Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob\" \\\n  --agent-dir agent \\\n  --branch dev\n```\n\nSkips K8s, task controller, task executor, git writeback. Useful for iterating on prompts.\n\n## Links\n\nAdmin endpoints:\n- Dev: <https://dev.quant.benjamin-borbe.de/admin/defect-diagnoser-agent/setloglevel/3>\n- Prod: <https://prod.quant.benjamin-borbe.de/admin/defect-diagnoser-agent/setloglevel/3>\n\n## Related\n\n- `pkg/prompts/` — embedded prompts (`workflow.md`, `output-format.md`)\n- `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md` — default agent guardrails\n- `docs/observation-scripts.md` — contract for the read-only observation scripts\n- `docs/claude-oauth-setup.md` — seed PVC with Claude Code OAuth credentials\n- `lib/claude/` — shared prompt assembly + Claude CLI invocation\n- `lib/delivery/` — shared Kafka result publishing\n- `task/controller/` — Obsidian→Kafka event source\n- `task/executor/` — Kafka→K8s Job spawner\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":63,"oldLines":6,"newStart":63,"newLines":28,"lines":[" "," Prefer constrained `Bash(path:*)` forms over bare `Bash` to minimize shell attack surface."," ","+### Service → repo mapping","+","+The diagnoser owns no mapping data. The operator supplies one entry per service","+through the existing `ENV_CONTEXT` channel, in the form","+`service_repo.<service>=<owner>/<repo>` — comma-separated when there is more","+than one:","+","+```","+ENV_CONTEXT=service_repo.checkout=acme/checkout,service_repo.billing=acme/billing","+```","+","+Each entry renders into the prompt's `## Environment` section as","+`service_repo.<service>: <owner>/<repo>`. A service resolves **only** on an","+exact, case-sensitive key match: no fuzzy match, no fallback, and no repo taken","+from the model's own knowledge. An unmapped service escalates to the operator","+instead of guessing.","+","+This mapping is deliberately **not** committed to this repo's `k8s/` Config —","+it is environment-specific operator input. The deterministic rules the binary","+enforces on top of it (the verdict block, the gate, the line guard and the","+heading rule) are documented in `docs/verdict-gate.md`.","+"," ### Claude subprocess env allowlist"," "," `lib/claude/claude-runner.go` strips pod env down to a safe allowlist (`HOME,PATH,USER,TZ,...`) before spawning `claude`, so a variable visible in `kubectl describe pod` can still be absent from the subprocess. Custom env vars (API URLs, credentials) **must** be passed through `CLAUDE_ENV` — a comma-separated `KEY=VALUE` list set on the Config's `spec.env` (or `-claude-env` for a local run) and parsed by both entry points. Don't expect pod env to reach Claude by default."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
