{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_42880ecfa4ad47569a8ac2f3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a64c526a94fed5f7","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/workspace/CHANGELOG.md","old_string":"- feat: Wire the observation scripts' endpoints through `CLAUDE_ENV` and align the Config allowlist, image and prose with the four scripts that exist [drops the non-existent `pod-logs.sh` entry, adds `git` to the runtime image, and adds `pkg/scripts/consistency_test.go` to fail `make test` when the allowlist, the scripts on disk and the docs disagree]","new_string":"- feat: Wire the observation scripts' endpoints through `CLAUDE_ENV` and align the Config allowlist, image and prose with the four scripts that exist [drops the non-existent `pod-logs.sh` entry, adds `git` to the runtime image, and adds `pkg/scripts/consistency_test.go` to fail `make test` when the allowlist, the scripts on disk and the docs disagree]\n- feat: Route `defect-diagnose` tasks to the three-phase diagnoser with the verdict gate and heading rule wrapped around each phase, retire the generic `llm` task type, and document the operator-supplied `service_repo.<service>` mapping [proves the wired chain end to end against a fake model, covering the happy path, confidence escalations, line-guard and `defect_id` rejections, and forged headings in every phase]"}}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65223de2-d5ca-493e-b6ca-024741641a7c","uuid":"5210f66f-838a-48a0-9a03-a1a77cc00dff","timestamp":"2026-11-26T19:06:39.228Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a64c526a94fed5f7","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/CHANGELOG.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65223de2-d5ca-493e-b6ca-024741641a7c","uuid":"d3f2cfc4-cea6-4b84-bca1-3e39a38cae89","timestamp":"2026-11-26T19:06:39.248Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/CHANGELOG.md","oldString":"- feat: Wire the observation scripts' endpoints through `CLAUDE_ENV` and align the Config allowlist, image and prose with the four scripts that exist [drops the non-existent `pod-logs.sh` entry, adds `git` to the runtime image, and adds `pkg/scripts/consistency_test.go` to fail `make test` when the allowlist, the scripts on disk and the docs disagree]","newString":"- feat: Wire the observation scripts' endpoints through `CLAUDE_ENV` and align the Config allowlist, image and prose with the four scripts that exist [drops the non-existent `pod-logs.sh` entry, adds `git` to the runtime image, and adds `pkg/scripts/consistency_test.go` to fail `make test` when the allowlist, the scripts on disk and the docs disagree]\n- feat: Route `defect-diagnose` tasks to the three-phase diagnoser with the verdict gate and heading rule wrapped around each phase, retire the generic `llm` task type, and document the operator-supplied `service_repo.<service>` mapping [proves the wired chain end to end against a fake model, covering the happy path, confidence escalations, line-guard and `defect_id` rejections, and forged headings in every phase]","originalFile":"# Changelog\n\nAll notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.\n\nPlease choose versions by [Semantic Versioning](http://semver.org/).\n\n* MAJOR version when you make incompatible API changes,\n* MINOR version when you add functionality in a backwards-compatible manner, and\n* PATCH version when you make backwards-compatible bug fixes.\n\n## Unreleased\n\n- feat: Add `agent/scripts/repo-clone.sh`, the fourth read-only observation script, cloning a public GitHub repo into the fixed `repos/` directory beside `scripts/` and reporting `clone_path`, `head_sha` and `default_branch` [rejects any reference that is not `owner/name`, resolves the destination with symlinks followed and refuses anything outside `repos/` before git runs or the filesystem is touched, then makes the clone non-writable]\n- feat: Wire the observation scripts' endpoints through `CLAUDE_ENV` and align the Config allowlist, image and prose with the four scripts that exist [drops the non-existent `pod-logs.sh` entry, adds `git` to the runtime image, and adds `pkg/scripts/consistency_test.go` to fail `make test` when the allowlist, the scripts on disk and the docs disagree]\n\n## v0.2.2\n\n- chore: remove orphaned section comments left in `.trivyignore` by the stale-ignore sweep\n\n## v0.2.1\n\n- chore: remove 9 stale vulnerability ignores (withdrawn advisory, module absent from go.mod, or version outside the affected range)\n- chore: install Trivy from a pinned release tarball in CI so the job no longer depends on the retired apt-key helper\n\n## v0.2.0\n\n- feat: add a `check-task-link` gate that fails a PR whose body carries no `Task: <task_identifier>` line, and install Trivy from the upstream script so `test` stops failing on the retired keyring helper\n\n## v0.1.5\n\n- chore: bump `ERRCHECK_VERSION` to v1.30.0 and `GOSEC_VERSION` to v2.30.0. The pinned versions could not type-check the Go 1.27 stdlib, and these stay in step with the canonical `tools.env`.\n\n## v0.1.4\n\n- chore: update Go to 1.27.4 and github.com/bborbe/agent to v0.141.1, github.com/bborbe/cqrs to v0.6.16, github.com/bborbe/errors to v1.6.7, github.com/bborbe/kafka to v1.29.14, github.com/bborbe/sentry to v1.10.8, github.com/bborbe/service to v1.11.4, github.com/bborbe/time to v1.27.28, github.com/bborbe/vault-cli to v0.192.4\n\n## v0.1.3\n\n- chore: restate the do-not-merge contract in the gate workflow\n\n## v0.1.2\n\n- chore: update github.com/bborbe/agent to v0.138.0, github.com/bborbe/cqrs to v0.6.15, github.com/bborbe/errors to v1.6.6, github.com/bborbe/kafka to v1.29.11, github.com/bborbe/sentry to v1.10.7, github.com/bborbe/service to v1.11.2, github.com/bborbe/time to v1.27.25, github.com/bborbe/vault-cli to v0.186.1, github.com/onsi/ginkgo/v2 to v2.34.0\n\n## v0.1.1\n\n- chore: update github.com/bborbe/agent to v0.103.1, github.com/bborbe/cqrs to v0.6.12, github.com/bborbe/errors to v1.6.3, github.com/bborbe/kafka to v1.28.3, github.com/bborbe/sentry to v1.10.5, github.com/bborbe/service to v1.11.0, github.com/bborbe/time to v1.27.17, github.com/bborbe/vault-cli to v0.174.1, github.com/onsi/ginkgo/v2 to v2.33.1, github.com/onsi/gomega to v1.44.0, github.com/prometheus/client_golang to v1.25.0\n\n## v0.1.0\n\n- fix: **Go 1.27.2 now passes `make precommit`.** The standalone `errcheck:` and `gosec:` targets are both retired and dropped from `check:`, and both linters now run embedded in golangci-lint, which `.golangci.yml` already enabled. `GOLANGCI_LINT_VERSION` moves v2.13.1 → v2.14.0, the `go` directive and `Dockerfile` move to 1.27.2, and `golang.org/x/net` moves v0.58.0 → v0.60.0. ⚠️ **Neither target was repairable, which is why both are removed rather than repointed.** `go run github.com/kisielk/errcheck@v1.20.0` and `go run github.com/securego/gosec/v2/cmd/gosec@$(GOSEC_VERSION)` each build in their **own** module context, pinning a `golang.org/x/tools` reader that stops at export-data version 4 while the 1.27.2 toolchain emits version 5, so each dies with `internal error: package \"X\" without types was imported` at any `go.mod` directive. Dropping the `@$(ERRCHECK_VERSION)` pin does not rescue it either: `precommit` runs `ensure` → `go mod tidy` first, and tidy strips a require nothing imports. ⚠️ **Coverage is preserved, not traded away.** `.golangci.yml` gains `settings.errcheck.exclude-functions` carrying the retired target's `-ignore '(Close|Write|Fprint)'` list, and `settings.gosec.excludes: [G104]` carrying `-exclude=G104`. The `go` directive bump is load-bearing rather than tidy: it is what clears the nine `stdlib@v1.27.1 -> v1.27.2` advisories that `osv-scanner` reports, and it could not move while the standalone targets ran. Also bumps `osv-scanner` v2.3.1 → v2.6.0: the pinned v2.3.1 panics during call-graph analysis in `golang.org/x/tools@v0.38.0/go/ssa`, and v2.6.0 carries a fixed x/tools.\n\n## v0.0.0\n\n- Initial scaffold from bborbe/agent-claude template via /launch-agent on 2026-09-27\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":12,"oldLines":6,"newStart":12,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," - feat: Add `agent/scripts/repo-clone.sh`, the fourth read-only observation script, cloning a public GitHub repo into the fixed `repos/` directory beside `scripts/` and reporting `clone_path`, `head_sha` and `default_branch` [rejects any reference that is not `owner/name`, resolves the destination with symlinks followed and refuses anything outside `repos/` before git runs or the filesystem is touched, then makes the clone non-writable]"," - feat: Wire the observation scripts' endpoints through `CLAUDE_ENV` and align the Config allowlist, image and prose with the four scripts that exist [drops the non-existent `pod-logs.sh` entry, adds `git` to the runtime image, and adds `pkg/scripts/consistency_test.go` to fail `make test` when the allowlist, the scripts on disk and the docs disagree]","+- feat: Route `defect-diagnose` tasks to the three-phase diagnoser with the verdict gate and heading rule wrapped around each phase, retire the generic `llm` task type, and document the operator-supplied `service_repo.<service>` mapping [proves the wired chain end to end against a fake model, covering the happy path, confidence escalations, line-guard and `defect_id` rejections, and forged headings in every phase]"," "," ## v0.2.2"," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
